Description: NexusOS: "Default layout" menu on the manual partitioning page
 Standard: plans EFI, /boot, swap and / on the selected disk with the auto-partitioning
 code (pending, editable; nothing is written until the installation starts).
 LVM: asks for root filesystem and sizes, prepares the disk with nexusos-lvm-layout
 (EFI, /boot, volume group "nexus" with swap and root, free space for more volumes),
 rescans and assigns mount points from the NexusOS filesystem labels.
Author: NexusOS contributors
Forwarded: not-needed
